---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
---

<ContentLayout
  title="About Crypto Made Easy"
  description="How the 3-Light checklist, position-sizing ladder, and interactive chart lessons work, plus our privacy and educational disclaimers."
>
  <p>
    <strong>Crypto Made Easy</strong> is a static, English-language learning course and manual
    signal checklist built for casual spot swing traders. When you open an exchange screen like
    Gate.com, the wall of moving averages, oscillators, and blinking order books can cause visual
    blindness and emotional panic selling.
  </p>

  <p>
    Our core promise is <strong>ease of mind</strong>: before placing any spot order, you know where
    the support floor is, how much USDT reserve remains unspent, and where the plan is invalidated.
  </p>

  <h2>Two Pillars</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Interactive Learn Modules:</strong> Eight short chapters with manipulable chart
      diagrams that explain how order books create candlesticks, volume, and indicators.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>3-Light Signal Checker:</strong> Type in the numbers from your 4H or 1D chart to
      evaluate Price vs MA30/BOLL, RSI, and Order Book Bid %, paired with an automatic 13% / 21% /
      30% split-entry ladder and 36% cash reserve.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="disclaimer">Educational Disclaimer &amp; Risk Notice</h2>
  <p>
    This application is an educational checklist and arithmetic calculator,{' '}
    <strong>not financial, investment, or trading advice</strong>. It does not predict market prices
    or guarantee outcomes. A 3-of-3 "Buy Zone" reading can still fail in a macro downtrend, which is
    why every plan requires a pre-agreed Stop-Loss ("Plan Broken") level below lowest support.
  </p>
  <p>
    Dated price figures for BTC, ETH, and SOL (from 5–6 November 2026) appear strictly as historical
    worked examples from the source documentation, never as live trading recommendations.
  </p>

  <h2 id="privacy">Statelessness &amp; Zero-Tracking Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    The Signal Checker is completely stateless: no backend, no user accounts, no cookies, and no
    analytics. Nothing you type into the Signal Checker is saved or leaves your browser; refreshing
    the page clears all checker inputs immediately. Only your optional chapter completion checkmarks
    are stored locally in your browser under <code>cme:v1</code> and can be reset at any time.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
